    "blocks_tibAtJ": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_0029bb1_KcYBnV": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_0029bb1",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The diamond clarity chart",
            "text": "<p>A diamond clarity chart is a grading scale used to describe the presence and visibility of inclusions and blemishes within a diamond. The most widely recognised clarity grading system was developed by the Gemological Institute of America (GIA), an independent non-profit institute established in 1931 and regarded as a global authority in gemmological research, education and diamond grading. </p><p>The GIA clarity scale includes six main categories, divided into 11 grades:</p><p><strong>Flawless (FL):</strong> No inclusions or blemishes visible under 10x magnification.</p><p><strong>Internally Flawless (IF):</strong> No inclusions visible under 10x magnification.</p><p><strong>Very, Very Slightly Included (VVS1 and VVS2):</strong> Inclusions are extremely difficult for a skilled grader to detect under 10x magnification.</p><p><strong>Very Slightly Included (VS1 and VS2):</strong> Minor inclusions are visible with effort under 10x magnification.</p><p><strong>Slightly Included (SI1 and SI2):</strong> Inclusions are noticeable under 10x magnification.</p><p><strong>Included (I1, I2 and I3): </strong>Inclusions are obvious under 10x magnification and may affect transparency, brilliance or durability.</p><p>To the naked eye, diamonds from different clarity grades can sometimes appear very similar. However, their differences can be significant in terms of rarity, value and overall quality. This is why careful assessment, certification and an understanding of the clarity scale are essential when selecting a diamond.</p>",
            "heading_size_desktop": 30,
            "text_size_desktop": 18,
            "padding_left_desktop": 380,
            "padding_right_desktop": 380,
            "spacing_desktop": 40,
            "heading_size_mobile": 20,
            "text_size_mobile": 14,
            "padding_left_mobile": 40,
            "padding_right_mobile": 40,
            "spacing_mobile": 20,
            "text_alignment": "center",
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "text_color": "#000000"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
